msgid "Logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:5
#: 9f241fc5562845beb98a9c9ac8ecf287
msgid "When Problems Arise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:7
#: 92dca5a4bd0c4fa6a06e737cb4d8be79
msgid "ArduPilot, is extremely capable and flexible. But with high performance and flexibility comes a lot of configurations, parameters, and complexity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:9
#: 59bd08fe25104bea8057d988345e0f85
msgid "This WIKI documentation attempts to reduce the effort of configuring and operating your ArduPilot based vehicle by providing as much accurate information on configuration, parameters, and operating modes as possible, and is continuously being updated as new releases occur or areas needing further explanation arise. Your assistance in that effort is welcomed and solicited. See :ref:`common_wiki_editing_guide`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:11
#: d588ce2345b549859eac2c628707d2f6
msgid "Enabling and using the logging capability of ArduPilot is usually a key requirement when seeking assistance from other in diagnosing issues that you cannot resolve yourself by following the suggestions below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:20
#: e40087cda8884473a4a8b272bf0c7886
msgid "What to do if you have an issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:22
#: ba73c8bc1fae4d5891c916759d7ad2d1
msgid "Make sure you have followed the vehicle's \"First Time Setup\" and \"First Flight/Drive\" Sections and carefully read the provided documentation. If dealing with advanced configuration or hardware options, thoroughly read the appropriate documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:24
#: 238e216dcff64f7e91868c3f67b53f58
msgid "If this does not help you resolve the issue, then seek help on the `Discuss Forum <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/>`__ section appropriate to your vehicle or ground station. Do not enter issues on the GitHub software repositories unless it has been confirmed as an actual issue in the code or documentation. Support will be given in the appropriate Discuss Forum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:26
#: f96aba23bb7f439899a57594e8f4ba21
msgid "Having a :Ref:`dataflash log <common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs>` will help you, or someone helping you, to diagnose the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:28
#: bd5857993da64880aad8e053dd1badd3
msgid "WatchDog resets (\"WDG:\") should be reported `on this page <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues/15915>`_ , Internal Errors (\"Internal Error:\") should be reported `here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues/15916>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:32
#: c5cf2c745942498b959bb7362cb9ec13
msgid "Vehicle Will Not Arm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:34
#: 0222d600c6534f06ab25015563917c71
msgid "See :ref:`common-prearm-safety-checks`. Do not disable arming checks except for bench setup testing. Doing so puts your vehicle at risk for a crash. Always track down the reason why a pre-arm check failure is occurring and correct it before operating the vehicle!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:37
#: 2322fce100b64ab5a11af7bba0ab0c3d
msgid "Interference issues on Electric Vehicles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:39
#: 6f2006f0315f4b88943f79d4b30333bf
msgid "Routing high current carrying wiring for motors in close proximity to ESCs or Servo Control wiring can result in interference with those peripherals controls due to electromagnetic coupling. Below is a video of aileron servos having their operation disrupted due to induced noise from adjacent motor high current wiring:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:45
#: bfa4a22a06b2489cba3f38da0c080454
msgid "This can be resolved by separating the power conducting and the signaling wiring by several inches or by using a more noise tolerant servo such as DroneCAN servos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:47
#: 10389d4bf28a4415a88b7c50b33b197b
msgid "See also :ref:`common-esc-issues` for similar issues with ESCs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:53
#: 471c577dcd78475aa1b1f829578feb12
msgid "Free RAM issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:55
#: 118aa4b0ac1d4c7f99def77a1bbf66b3
msgid "During initialization, it is possible for some features/subsystems to fail to get enough RAM allocated. Sometimes this will be announced such as in the case of insufficient memory to start a LUA script: \"Scripting requires a larger minimum stack size\", or for terrain: \"Terrain: Allocation failed\", etc. Also, insufficient free memory can result in compass calibration failing or MAVftp not initializing. See  :ref:`RAM Limitations <ram_limitations>` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:58
#: e2ca2c1e55ab4beebc5827ae49c96eec
msgid "H7 AutoPilot Will Not Initialize"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:60
#: 210fb5589e0b428bb556b10fbd65431f
msgid "AutoPilots utilizing the H7 series of processors can, on rare occasions, get into a state where they will no longer complete initialization. Symptoms are: never exiting the bootloader (rapidly flashing led right after power application never stops) or the autopilot freezes during initialization, and connection to it is impossible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:62
#: ebc933b39d124a58be5f2148e568899e
msgid "It is believed that this may be a memory corruption problem which can be caused by interrupting a flash memory write (as when changing parameters). Unfortunately, due to the processor's architecture, there is no way in the firmware to correct this automatically. If the autopilot  seems \"bricked\", try this to completely reset the autopilot to a fully un-programmed state. This should allow the firmware to be installed and the corruption issue resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:64
#: 0ce8fb10c6334b2e8bfae6b667c92461
msgid "First, program the entire 2MB flash space with zeros by loading `this file <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/STM32-tools/2MByte_allzero.bin>`_ which contains all zero data. Use the instructions :ref:`here <common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards>` but use the above file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:66
#: 8926e220e06b413a82a7a3ee00f4ecc6
msgid "Next, download the ArduPilot bootloader for your AutoPilot from `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/Bootloaders/>`__. Then repeat the above step using that bootloader file. This will place the bootloader on the autopilot. Cycle the power on the autopilot. At this point it will power up and remain in the bootloader until operational firmware is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:68
#: 63dc92f5b5f54004a8e3e3969c2a1f5a
msgid "Finally, use Mission Planner's SETUP/Install Firmware tab or the `Uploader <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/master/Tools/scripts/uploader.py>`__ python script, to load the desired ArduPilot firmware revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-when-problems-arise.rst:70
#: 003609ca5ad041ee9204bcd33c7eece9
msgid "This should resolve issues caused by memory corruption and normal operation will resume."
msgstr ""
